    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_value\",\n      \"components\": [\"U2\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U2.1\", \"U2.2\", \"U2.3\", \"U2.4\", \"U2.5\", \"U2.24\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"+3.3V\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"PCA9685PW address pin A0 (U2 pin 1) is on the +3.3V net, while A1\u2013A5 (pins 2, 3, 4, 5, 24) are all on GND. This sets the A0 address bit high.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The spec lists the PWM driver at I2C address 0x40, which requires all address-select pins to be low. A0 should be tied to GND like the other address pins.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U2\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"A0\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U2\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"A1\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"With A0 high, the PCA9685 responds at 0x41, not 0x40. The FCC firmware cannot reach the servo PWM driver, so no servo outputs are produced.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.6\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"bridged_nets\",\n      \"components\": [\"FCC1\", \"UART3_FCC1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"FCC1.73\", \"FCC1.48\", \"UART3_FCC1.3\", \"UART3_FCC1.4\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"UART3_RX_FCC\", \"UART3_TX_FCC\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The UART3 signals are connected to FCC1 pins 73 and 48, which the MCU library defines as VCAP (internal regulator decoupling pins, power_out). The UART3 signals are not on the peripheral USART pins.\",\n      \"expected\": \"UART3 TX/RX should be routed to USART-capable GPIO pins. VCAP pins must carry only the regulator decoupling capacitor, and no signal should be connected to them.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"144\\\") (name \\\"UART3_RX_FCC\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"73\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VCAP\\\") (pintype \\\"power_out\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"48\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VCAP\\\") (pintype \\\"power_out\\\"))\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The UART3 link is unusable, and driving signals onto the VCAP regulator pins can disturb the core regulator. Decoupling capacitor C13 is also left with a floating pin, so the VCAP network is not properly formed.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.35\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The PCA9685 address-select pin A0 is tied high to +3.3V while the spec requires address 0x40 with all select pins low, so the PWM driver would respond at 0x41. The UART3 nets are also wired to the VCAP pins of the H753, which is a second likely deviation.\"\n}",
